+# Source, topology, and bounded novelty audit
+
+Checked September 30, 2026. The exact frozen candidate counterexample passed separate adversarial review; priority has not been established.
+
+## Exact target
+
+The complete pinned record was read after the live problem page proved inaccessible to the web reader. The full original [OWR report](https://ems.press/doi/pdf/10.4171/OWR/2017/3) was downloaded and Belegradek's contribution, printed pp. 148–151, read in context; p. 149 was rendered and visually checked. The event was in January 2017; the publisher's page lists publication on January 3, 2018. This explains the report-year/publication-year variation in the imported citation.
+
+The metrics are smooth and complete with nonnegative curvature. The normalized orientation-preserving diffeomorphisms fix 0 and 1 on the plane, or 0, 1 and infinity on the sphere. The function factor is restricted to conformal metrics satisfying the same curvature and completeness requirements. The problem concerns continuity in weaker topologies on these smooth objects, not the existence of uniformizing maps for merely continuous metrics.
+
+The exact derivative shift is unambiguous in the full primary references: metrics and functions have C^r topology, while diffeomorphisms have C^(r+1) topology. The workshop's action notation is abbreviated; switching between pullback by a diffeomorphism and pushforward by its inverse does not change the question, since inversion is a homeomorphism of these C^(r+1) diffeomorphism groups. The candidate follows the dataset and Banakh–Belegradek's pullback convention.
+
+## Earlier theorem and actual correction
+
+The full two-page [Belegradek–Hu erratum](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00208-015-1354-1), Math. Ann. 364 (2016), 711–712, was downloaded from the publisher and read. It corrects the earlier integer-topology homeomorphism assertion by inserting a Hölder exponent 0<alpha<1 at every regularity index. It explains that the applied continuity theorem was available in Hölder rather than integer topology. At that time the authors suspected failure at the integer endpoint but had no counterexamples. The erratum explicitly says the paper's other results were unaffected.
+
+The current [Banakh–Belegradek preprint](https://arxiv.org/abs/1510.07269) is v2, March 1, 2017; v1 dates to October 25, 2015. Sections 2, 8 and 9 provide the topologies, normalizations, and corrected homeomorphism statements. The work was published in J. Math. Soc. Japan 70 (2018), 733–756, [DOI 10.2969/jmsj/07027344](https://doi.org/10.2969/jmsj/07027344). The primary proof audit here uses the accessible arXiv version; the publisher metadata independently confirms publication. There is no reliance on the superseded integer-topology claim.
+
+## Scope of the candidate
+
+The candidate gives separate sequences for r=0, r=1, and every r>=2. It preserves the exact geometric constraints, and in fact uses positive-curvature metrics. The r=1 argument includes a nonlinear curvature-sign estimate: C^1 convergence alone is never used to infer curvature control. The conclusion is failure of the specified parametrization to be a homeomorphism. It does not classify the abstract homeomorphism type of the metric space and does not contradict the noninteger Hölder or C^infinity results.
+
+The construction's normalization is explicit rather than achieved by uncontrolled postcomposition. Its conformal factors are defined by an exact pullback identity; completeness and curvature of those factors follow by isometry. On the noncompact plane all perturbations lie in a fixed disk, so compact-open versus global uniform control creates no escape-to-infinity issue.
+
+## Prior attempts, duplicates, and novelty limits
+
+Before research there was no own attempt folder, matching remote branch, numeric-ID PR, state record, or related-target-group entry. An all-state descriptive PR search found only the unrelated conformal-primitive PR22. A pinned-corpus search found no other record with this exact conformal-metric parametrization target. The queue row was rank73, queued, 0/5.
+
+Current-source searches used the exact paper title, the authors' names with integer topology and counterexample terms, and conformal-parametrization endpoint terms. The authoritative material recovered was the original expectation and the erratum. No later resolution was identified in this bounded search. This does not establish priority: slow radial twists and logarithmic failures of endpoint regularity are standard mechanisms. The candidate must remain priority-unconfirmed and AI-reviewed/unrefereed even if its separate mathematical audit passes.
